    Fix cr-jl4fix1-2: a retry's raw names travel as bytes from any host

    A retry turned a failed non-UTF-8 name into a path only on Unix, so a
    Windows client retrying such a file on a remote Unix source sent its
    lossy text and matched nothing. A retry now keeps those names as their
    bytes from the record to the wire filter, on every host; only a local
    source that can hold such names turns them into paths.

